      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The area was ancestral land of the Kaw (Kansa) Nation, whose Siouan-speaking people lived along the Kansas River long before European contact.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/williamstown_kansas",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Upland prairie here is dominated by big bluestem and switchgrass, while riparian zones near the river host cottonwood, willow, and sedges.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/williamstown_kansas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Williamstown Historical Museum showcases nine historic site markers across town, inviting visitors to explore the community’s heritage.",
